<title>GREECE: Greek avg 1996 CPI seen down to 8.3 pct -minister.</title>
<headline>Greek avg 1996 CPI seen down to 8.3 pct -minister.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek National Economy Minister Yannos Papandoniou said the average CPI inflation should fall to 8.3 percent in 1996 from 9.3 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>He said the average rate on the marker 12-month T-bill is expected to ease to 12.7 percent from 15.5 percent last year.</p>
</text>
